# ADR 0005: Local notifications only, no backend

**Date:** 2026-08-02
**Status:** Accepted

## Context
FORGE needs notifications for rest timer completion, workout 
reminders, and (potentially) PR celebrations. Remote push requires 
a backend server; local notifications run entirely on-device.

## Decision
Use only local notifications (UNUserNotificationCenter). No backend.

## Alternatives considered
- **Remote push (APNs):** Requires server infrastructure, 
  device-token management, and privacy manifest additions. No 
  feature currently justifies the cost.

## Consequences
- Zero backend infrastructure for v1.
- All notifications must be scheduled ahead of time or fired from 
  a running app instance (including the Watch extension).
- If a future feature requires cross-device or server-initiated 
  notifications, this decision needs revisiting.

